{
  "title": "Da bambino {im:giocavo} spesso al mare",
  "translation": "As a child I often played at the seaside",
  "topics": "The imperfetto: habits, descriptions and actions in progress in the past",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      {
        "h": "What the imperfetto is for"
      },
      "The *imperfetto* looks at the past from the inside, without saying when something started or ended. It has three main uses.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Use",
            "Example",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Habits",
              "Da bambino {im:giocavo} spesso.",
              "As a child I often played."
            ],
            [
              "Descriptions",
              "La casa {im:era} piccola.",
              "The house was small."
            ],
            [
              "Actions in progress",
              "{im:Leggevo} un libro.",
              "I was reading a book."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "How to form it"
      },
      "Take the infinitive, remove the final *-re*, and add the same endings for all three groups. The vowel of the infinitive stays, so you don't have to learn three patterns.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "",
            "parlare",
            "leggere",
            "dormire"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "io",
              "{im:parla**vo**}",
              "{im:legge**vo**}",
              "{im:dormi**vo**}"
            ],
            [
              "tu",
              "{im:parla**vi**}",
              "{im:legge**vi**}",
              "{im:dormi**vi**}"
            ],
            [
              "lui / lei",
              "{im:parla**va**}",
              "{im:legge**va**}",
              "{im:dormi**va**}"
            ],
            [
              "noi",
              "{im:parla**vamo**}",
              "{im:legge**vamo**}",
              "{im:dormi**vamo**}"
            ],
            [
              "voi",
              "{im:parla**vate**}",
              "{im:legge**vate**}",
              "{im:dormi**vate**}"
            ],
            [
              "loro",
              "{im:parla**vano**}",
              "{im:legge**vano**}",
              "{im:dormi**vano**}"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "The few irregular verbs"
      },
      "*Essere* is truly irregular. *Fare*, *bere* and *dire* only use their longer old stems, with the normal endings.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "",
            "essere",
            "fare",
            "bere",
            "dire"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "io",
              "{im:ero}",
              "{im:fa**ce**vo}",
              "be**ve**vo",
              "{im:di**ce**vo}"
            ],
            [
              "tu",
              "{im:eri}",
              "{im:fa**ce**vi}",
              "be**ve**vi",
              "{im:di**ce**vi}"
            ],
            [
              "lui / lei",
              "{im:era}",
              "{im:fa**ce**va}",
              "be**ve**va",
              "{im:di**ce**va}"
            ],
            [
              "noi",
              "{im:eravamo}",
              "{im:fa**ce**vamo}",
              "be**ve**vamo",
              "{im:di**ce**vamo}"
            ],
            [
              "voi",
              "{im:eravate}",
              "{im:fa**ce**vate}",
              "be**ve**vate",
              "{im:di**ce**vate}"
            ],
            [
              "loro",
              "{im:erano}",
              "{im:fa**ce**vano}",
              "be**ve**vano",
              "{im:di**ce**vano}"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "Words that often go with it"
      },
      "*Da bambino* (as a child), *di solito* (usually), *ogni estate* (every summer), *sempre* (always), *spesso* (often), *mentre* (while)."
    ]
  },
